     "<p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">There has been a reworking of the batch files for upcoming version 0.7 . The new files are:</p><ul style=\"padding-left:25px;max-width:62em;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><li style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:0.3em\"><a href=\"https://batchfiles.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/R.bat\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://batchfiles.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/R.bat&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489597702000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-kvQIFD12K4aoeJGwo3zA\">R.bat</a> - configuration free way to run R. Try. <tt style=\"font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;max-width:66em\">R.bat help</tt> for concise help and examples</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:0.3em\"><a href=\"https://batchfiles.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/Rpathset.bat\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://batchfiles.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/Rpathset.bat&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489597702000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3MRlH5w0yb3tjPxIrEu0HY\">Rpathset.bat</a><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"> - unlike  </font><span style=\"font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px\">R.bat, </span><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">which is configuration free this, is manually set up through </font><font face=\"Monaco, DejaVu Sans Mono, Bitstream Vera Sans Mono, Lucida Console, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">SET </span></font><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">statements.</span></li><li style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:0.3em\"><a href=\"https://batchfiles.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/batchfiles.md\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://batchfiles.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/batchfiles.md&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489597702000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1mxFIwD1TRA3_DI8a-J--D\">batchfiles.md</a> - detailed documenation. Can read it as is or use <tt style=\"font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;max-width:66em\">pandoc batchfiles.md -o batchfiles.pdf</tt> to get a pdf version.</li></ul><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\">batchfiles is a collection of Windows .bat, .js and .hta files used for running R under Windows.  They are each self contained and independent of each other. Just place any on your Windows path to use it.  See <a href=\"http://batchfiles.googlecode.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://batchfiles.googlecode.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489597702000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0-GlbHsYT5AOSDUJrSfGFI\">http://batchfiles.googlecode.com</a></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\">Feedback can be reported to this discussion group.</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\"><br></span></font></div>"
